{"id":"80b1e399f31271a65b4cfbac98bd9d8871482463","axis":"silent","repo":"linq2db/linq2db","sha":"80b1e399f31271a65b4cfbac98bd9d8871482463","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".github/workflows/build.yml","lines":["@@ -107,6 +107,10 @@ jobs:","             if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit $LASTEXITCODE }","           }"," ","+          # The browser build of LinqToDB is a separate instance that every package hook requests at once.","+          dotnet build Source/LinqToDB/LinqToDB.csproj @common -f net11.0 -p:BrowserWasmAssetBuild=true","+          if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit $LASTEXITCODE }","+","       # The API analyzers are a release-prep gate (/release-publicapi), not a per-PR one.","       - name: Build solution","         run: dotnet build ${{ env.SOLUTION }} --configuration ${{ env.RELEASE_CONFIGURATION }} -p:RunApiAnalyzersDuringBuild=false ${{ env.VERSION_ARGS }}","@@ -125,6 +129,10 @@ jobs:","         shell: pwsh","         run: ./Build/Azure/scripts/verify-analyzer-delivery.ps1 -PackagesDir .build/package/release -NoAzdoLogs"," ","+      - name: Verify browser-wasm assets","+        shell: pwsh","+        run: ./Build/Azure/scripts/verify-browser-wasm-asset.ps1 -PackagesDir .build/package/release -NoAzdoLogs","+","       # linq2db.cli, the 14 T4 packages and the LINQPad 5 .lpx physically redistribute third-party","       # binaries under an MIT license expression that covers only linq2db's own code. `check` catches a","       # hand-edited or un-regenerated notices file; `verify` opens the packed output and fails on a","@@ -279,7 +287,7 @@ jobs:","   wasm-tests:","     name: WASM runtime tests","     runs-on: ubuntu-24.04","-    timeout-minutes: 20","+    timeout-minutes: 90"," ","     steps:","       - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7.0.1"],"additions":9,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"Build/Azure/pipelines/templates/build-job.yml","lines":["@@ -217,6 +217,15 @@ jobs:","     displayName: Build Solution for Nuget","     condition: and(succeeded(), ${{ parameters.with_nugets }})"," ","+  # The browser build of LinqToDB is a separate instance that every package hook requests at once.","+  - task: DotNetCoreCLI@2","+    inputs:","+      command: build","+      projects: Source/LinqToDB/LinqToDB.csproj","+      arguments: -f net11.0 -property:BrowserWasmAssetBuild=true -property:RunAnalyzersDuringBuild=${{ variables['with_analyzers'] }} -property:RunApiAnalyzersDuringBuild=${{ variables['with_api_analyzers'] }} --configuration $(release_configuration)","+    displayName: Build LinqToDB browser asset","+    condition: and(succeeded(), ${{ parameters.with_nugets }})","+","   - task: DotNetCoreCLI@2","     inputs:","       command: custom","@@ -226,6 +235,14 @@ jobs:","     displayName: Pack Solution for Nuget","     condition: and(succeeded(), ${{ parameters.with_nugets }})"," ","+  - task: PowerShell@2","+    displayName: Verify browser-wasm assets","+    inputs:","+      pwsh: true","+      filePath: '$(Build.SourcesDirectory)/Build/Azure/scripts/verify-browser-wasm-asset.ps1'","+      arguments: '-PackagesDir \"$(Build.SourcesDirectory)/.build/package/release\"'","+    condition: and(succeeded(), ${{ parameters.with_nugets }})","+","   # These two live here rather than in nuget-job.yml, where the other pre-publish guards sit, for two","   # reasons. nuget-job only runs from the `default` pipeline (master/release and release-targeting PRs),","   # so a PR that pulls in a new bundled dependency would pass, merge, and only fail on master. And the"],"additions":17,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"Build/Azure/scripts/verify-browser-wasm-asset.ps1","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,142 @@","+<#","+verify-browser-wasm-asset.ps1 - assert the packages a browser app can load carry a Mono-compatible assembly.","+","+net11.0 assemblies are built with runtime-async, which Mono, the default browser-wasm runtime, cannot run. Each","+package below therefore carries a second build under runtimes/browser-wasm/lib/<tfm>/, produced by the","+AddBrowserWasmAssetToPackage target in Directory.Build.targets. Nothing else notices if that build stops being","+packed or starts being compiled with runtime-async: every server-side test passes either way.","+","+Checks, for each package in $Packages and each net11.0-or-newer lib/<tfm>/<id>.dll:","+  1. runtimes/browser-wasm/lib/<tfm>/<id>.dll exists.","+  2. It has no method with MethodImplAttributes.Async.","+  3. lib/<tfm>/<id>.dll does have such methods, so the check above can tell the two builds apart.","+","+Usage:","+","+  pwsh -NoProfile -File Build/Azure/scripts/verify-browser-wasm-asset.ps1 -PackagesDir <dir>","+","+  -PackagesDir   directory to scan recursively for *.nupkg (required)","+  -NoAzdoLogs    suppress the Azure DevOps `##vso[task.logissue]` lines, which are on by default. A switch rather","+                 than a [bool], because `pwsh -File` passes every argument as a string.","+","+Exit codes:","+  0  every check passed","+  1  a check failed","+  2  invalid args, or a listed package is absent from the drop","+#>","+","+param(","+    [Parameter(Mandatory = $true)]","+    [string] $PackagesDir,","+    [switch] $NoAzdoLogs","+)","+","+$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'","+","+$Packages = @('linq2db', 'linq2db.Remote.HttpClient.Client', 'linq2db.Remote.SignalR.Client', 'linq2db.Remote.Grpc')","+","+$MethodImplAsync = 0x2000","+","+function Write-Failure([string] $Message) {","+    if (-not $NoAzdoLogs) { Write-Host \"##vso[task.logissue type=error]$Message\" }","+    Write-Host \"FAIL: $Message\"","+}","+","+function Get-AsyncMethodCount([System.IO.Compression.ZipArchiveEntry] $Entry) {","+    $buffer = [System.IO.MemoryStream]::new()","+","+    $source = $Entry.Open()","+","+    try {","+        $source.CopyTo($buffer)","+    }","+    finally {","+        $source.Dispose()","+    }","+","+    $buffer.Position = 0","+","+    $reader = [System.Reflection.PortableExecutable.PEReader]::new($buffer)","+","+    try {","+        $metadata = [System.Reflection.Metadata.PEReaderExtensions]::GetMetadataReader($reader)","+        $count    = 0","+","+        foreach ($handle in $metadata.MethodDefinitions) {","+            if ([int]$metadata.GetMethodDefinition($handle).ImplAttributes -band $MethodImplAsync) {","+                $count++","+            }","+        }","+","+        return $count","+    }","+    finally {","+        $reader.Dispose()","+    }","+}","+","+if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $PackagesDir)) {","+    Write-Host \"PackagesDir '$PackagesDir' does not exist\"","+    exit 2","+}","+","+Add-Type -AssemblyName System.IO.Compression.FileSystem","+","+$nupkgs = @(Get-ChildItem -LiteralPath $PackagesDir -Recurse -Filter *.nupkg)","+$failed = $false","+","+foreach ($id in $Packages) {","+    $nupkg = $nupkgs | Where-Object { $_.Name -match ('^' + [regex]::Escape($id) + '\\.\\d') } | Select-Object -First 1","+","+    if (-not $nupkg) {","+        Write-Host \"Package '$id' not found under '$PackagesDir'\"","+        exit 2","+    }","+","+    $zip = [System.IO.Compression.ZipFile]::OpenRead($nupkg.FullName)","+","+    try {","+        $libs = @($zip.Entries | Where-Object { $_.FullName -match ('^lib/net(\\d+)\\.0/' + [regex]::Escape($id) + '\\.dll$') -and [int]$Matches[1] -ge 11 })","+","+        if ($libs.Count -eq 0) {","+            Write-Failure \"$id has no net11.0-or-newer lib asset\"","+            $failed = $true","+        }","+","+        foreach ($lib in $libs) {","+            $tfm      = $lib.FullName.Split('/')[1]","+            $assetPath = \"runtimes/browser-wasm/lib/$tfm/$id.dll\"","+            $asset    = $zip.GetEntry($assetPath)","+","+            if (-not $asset) {","+                Write-Failure \"$id has no $assetPath\"","+                $failed = $true","+                continue","+            }","+","+            $assetAsync = Get-AsyncMethodCount $asset","+            $libAsync   = Get-AsyncMethodCount $lib","+","+            if ($assetAsync -ne 0) {","+                Write-Failure \"$id $assetPath has $assetAsync runtime-async methods, expected 0\"","+                $failed = $true","+            }","+","+            if ($libAsync -eq 0) {","+                Write-Failure \"$id $($lib.FullName) has no runtime-async methods, so the build is not what this check assumes\"","+                $failed = $true","+            }","+","+            Write-Host \"$id ${tfm}: lib $libAsync runtime-async methods, browser-wasm $assetAsync\"","+        }","+    }","+    finally {","+        $zip.Dispose()","+    }","+}","+","+if ($failed) {","+    exit 1","+}","+","+exit 0"],"additions":142,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"Directory.Build.props","lines":["@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@"," \t\t<Configurations>Testing;Debug;Release;Azure</Configurations>"," "," \t\t<AppDesignerFolder>Properties</AppDesignerFolder>","-\t\t<LangVersion>14</LangVersion>","+\t\t<LangVersion>15</LangVersion>"," \t\t<Nullable>enable</Nullable>"," \t\t<WarningLevel>9999</WarningLevel>"," \t\t<ErrorReport>prompt</ErrorReport>","@@ -94,6 +94,7 @@"," "," \t\t<ArtifactsPath>$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory).build</ArtifactsPath>"," \t\t<ArtifactsPivots>$(Configuration)\\$(TargetFramework)\\$(RuntimeIdentifier)</ArtifactsPivots>","+\t\t<ArtifactsPivots Condition=\" '$(BrowserWasmAssetBuild)' == 'true' \">$(ArtifactsPivots)\\browser-asset</ArtifactsPivots>"," \t</PropertyGroup>"," "," \t<PropertyGroup Label=\"Nuget\">"],"additions":2,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"Directory.Build.targets","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@","+<Project xmlns=\"http://schemas.microsoft.com/developer/msbuild/2003\">","+","+\t<!-- .targets, not .props: a props file is evaluated before the project body, so $(TargetFramework)","+\t     is empty there for a project that declares a single TargetFramework in its own body, and the","+\t     condition silently never fires. Build without it with -p:UseRuntimeAsync=false -t:Rebuild:","+\t     $(Features) is not a CoreCompile input, so without -t:Rebuild the previous binary is reused.","+\t     Mono, the default browser-wasm runtime, cannot run runtime-async methods. -->","+\t<PropertyGroup>","+\t\t<UseRuntimeAsync Condition=\" '$(UseRuntimeAsync)' == '' and ('$(BrowserWasmAssetBuild)' == 'true' or '$(RuntimeIdentifier)' == 'browser-wasm') \">false</UseRuntimeAsync>","+\t\t<UseRuntimeAsync Condition=\" '$(UseRuntimeAsync)' == '' \">true</UseRuntimeAsync>","+\t\t<Features Condition=\" '$(UseRuntimeAsync)' == 'true' and $([MSBuild]::IsTargetFrameworkCompatible('$(TargetFramework)', 'net11.0')) \">$(Features);runtime-async=on</Features>","+\t</PropertyGroup>","+","+\t<!-- A package a browser app can load carries a second net11.0 build, without runtime-async. NuGet selects","+\t     runtimes/browser-wasm by RID: a net11.0-browser asset is never chosen by a plain net11.0 + browser-wasm app. -->","+\t<PropertyGroup Condition=\" '$(PackBrowserWasmAsset)' == 'true' and '$(BrowserWasmAssetBuild)' != 'true' and $([MSBuild]::IsTargetFrameworkCompatible('$(TargetFramework)', 'net11.0')) \">","+\t\t<TargetsForTfmSpecificContentInPackage>$(TargetsForTfmSpecificContentInPackage);AddBrowserWasmAssetToPackage</TargetsForTfmSpecificContentInPackage>","+\t</PropertyGroup>","+","+\t<Target Name=\"AddBrowserWasmAssetToPackage\">","+\t\t<MSBuild Projects=\"$(MSBuildProjectFullPath)\" Targets=\"Build\" Properties=\"TargetFramework=$(TargetFramework);BrowserWasmAssetBuild=true\">","+\t\t\t<Output TaskParameter=\"TargetOutputs\" ItemName=\"_BrowserWasmAsset\" />","+\t\t</MSBuild>","+","+\t\t<ItemGroup>","+\t\t\t<TfmSpecificPackageFile Include=\"@(_BrowserWasmAsset)\" PackagePath=\"runtimes/browser-wasm/lib/$(TargetFramework)/\" />","+\t\t</ItemGroup>","+\t</Target>","+","+</Project>"],"additions":30,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"Examples/Remote/HttpClient/HttpClientClient/HttpClientClient.csproj","lines":["@@ -7,7 +7,9 @@"," \t</PropertyGroup>"," "," \t<ItemGroup>","-\t\t<ProjectReference Include=\"..\\..\\..\\..\\Source\\LinqToDB.Remote.HttpClient.Client\\LinqToDB.Remote.HttpClient.Client.csproj\" />","+\t\t<!-- Blazor apps run on Mono, so both edges to linq2db need the build without runtime-async. -->","+\t\t<ProjectReference Include=\"..\\..\\..\\..\\Source\\LinqToDB.Remote.HttpClient.Client\\LinqToDB.Remote.HttpClient.Client.csproj\" AdditionalProperties=\"BrowserWasmAssetBuild=true\" />","+\t\t<ProjectReference Update=\"..\\..\\..\\..\\Source\\LinqToDB\\LinqToDB.csproj\" AdditionalProperties=\"BrowserWasmAssetBuild=true\" />"," "," \t\t<PackageReference Include=\"Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly\" />"," \t\t<PackageReference Include=\"Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.DevServer\" />"],"additions":3,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"Examples/Remote/SignalR/SignalRClient/SignalRClient.csproj","lines":["@@ -7,7 +7,9 @@"," \t</PropertyGroup>"," "," \t<ItemGroup>","-\t\t<ProjectReference Include=\"..\\..\\..\\..\\Source\\LinqToDB.Remote.SignalR.Client\\LinqToDB.Remote.SignalR.Client.csproj\" />","+\t\t<!-- Blazor apps run on Mono, so both edges to linq2db need the build without runtime-async. -->","+\t\t<ProjectReference Include=\"..\\..\\..\\..\\Source\\LinqToDB.Remote.SignalR.Client\\LinqToDB.Remote.SignalR.Client.csproj\" AdditionalProperties=\"BrowserWasmAssetBuild=true\" />","+\t\t<ProjectReference Update=\"..\\..\\..\\..\\Source\\LinqToDB\\LinqToDB.csproj\" AdditionalProperties=\"BrowserWasmAssetBuild=true\" />"," "," \t\t<PackageReference Include=\"Octonica.ClickHouseClient\" />"," \t\t<PackageReference Include=\"ClickHouse.Driver\" />"],"additions":3,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"Source/CodeGenerators/Directory.Build.props","lines":["@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@"," \t<PropertyGroup>"," \t\t<Configurations>Testing;Debug;Release;Azure</Configurations>"," \t\t","-\t\t<LangVersion>14</LangVersion>","+\t\t<LangVersion>15</LangVersion>"," \t\t<Nullable>enable</Nullable>"," \t\t<WarningLevel>9999</WarningLevel>"," \t\t<ErrorReport>prompt</ErrorReport>"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"Source/LinqToDB.FSharp/FSharpQueryExpressionInterceptor.fs","lines":["@@ -161,7 +161,7 @@ type private FSharpRewriteVisitor(mappingSchema: MappingSchema) =","                 | _ -> simplified <- false","                 i <- i - 1"," ","-            if simplified then this.Visit result |> nonNull","+            if simplified then this.Visit result","             else base.VisitBlock node","         else","             base.VisitBlock node","@@ -244,12 +244,12 @@ type private FSharpRewriteVisitor(mappingSchema: MappingSchema) =","                             |> nonNull","                         // Re-normalize any residual F# shapes, then wrap the way the translator's UnwrapLambda","                         // expects (it peels Quote/Convert, then casts to LambdaExpression).","-                        Some (Expression.Quote(this.Visit (replaced :?> LambdaExpression) |> nonNull))","+                        Some (Expression.Quote(this.Visit (replaced :?> LambdaExpression)))","                 | bare ->","                     // No captured variables: convert the quotation directly with F#'s own method.","                     let q   = this.Eval bare","                     let lam = (node.Method.InvokeExt(null, [| q |]) |> nonNull) :?> LambdaExpression","-                    Some (Expression.Quote(this.Visit lam |> nonNull))","+                    Some (Expression.Quote(this.Visit lam))","             // Fail safe: any unexpected shape/evaluation surprise leaves the node untouched (no worse than","             // before this rewrite existed), so only genuinely-matching F# quotation predicates are transformed.","             // A flatten-invariant violation raised by the nested Visit is not such a surprise - it must stay","@@ -377,7 +377,7 @@ type private FSharpRewriteVisitor(mappingSchema: MappingSchema) =","                             raise (FlattenInvariantException","                                        \"F# chained group join could not be flattened: the group join's inner sequence or a hoisted tail operator is correlated to the outer element. See https://github.com/linq2db/linq2db/issues/5790\")"," ","-                        Some (this.Visit flattened |> nonNull)","+                        Some (this.Visit flattened)","         // Stays broad: AsLambda's cast and the pair-type construction still signal an unsupported shape by","         // throwing (a non-lambda argument, a non-generic outer element). It therefore also swallows a genuine","         // rewrite bug, whose fallback here is the un-flattened INNER JOIN LATERAL shape - silent row loss.","@@ -414,6 +414,6 @@ type FSharpQueryExpressionInterceptor private () =","             // Only the raw, pre-expose query tree (standard nodes) - the post-expose tree carries","             // linq2db custom nodes the F# constructs we handle never appear in.","             if args.Kind = QueryExpressionArgs.ExpressionKind.Query then","-                FSharpRewriteVisitor(args.DataContext.MappingSchema).Visit expression |> nonNull","+                FSharpRewriteVisitor(args.DataContext.MappingSchema).Visit expression","             else","                 expression"],"additions":5,"deletions":5,"truncated":false},{"path":"Source/LinqToDB.FSharp/LinqToDB.FSharp.fsproj","lines":["@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@"," ﻿<Project Sdk=\"Microsoft.NET.Sdk\">"," "," \t<PropertyGroup>","-\t\t<LangVersion>9</LangVersion>","+\t\t<LangVersion>11</LangVersion>"," \t\t<AssemblyName>linq2db.FSharp</AssemblyName>"," \t\t<RootNamespace>LinqToDB.FSharp</RootNamespace>"," "],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"Source/LinqToDB.Remote.Grpc/LinqToDB.Remote.Grpc.csproj","lines":["@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@"," \t</PropertyGroup>"," "," \t<PropertyGroup Label=\"Nuget\">","+\t\t<PackBrowserWasmAsset>true</PackBrowserWasmAsset>"," \t\t<Title>LINQ to DB remote data context over gRPC</Title>"," \t\t<Description>LINQ to DB Remote gRPC